#1. 
Install UTM as a virtual box 
#2.
Download the Ubuntu server matching your devices chip 
#3. 
For Apple M1 chip devices download,: 
    mininet-2.3.0-210211-ubuntu-20.04.1-legacy-server-amd64-ovf.zip from github.com/mininet/mininet/releases
    Unzip to access .vmdk file 

#4. 
Create a New Virtual Machine 
   Select emulate, then select other
   Skip the ISO Boot  

#5. 
In UTM setup for Apple M1 devices ensure 
    Architecture is x86_64 
    System Standard PC (Q35)
    Memory 2048
    CPU cores 2 

Edit Settings After Creating 
    New drive -> set interface to IDE 
    UEFI Boot should not be checked 
    Leave display as default 

#6.
Name Mininet + Create Password 
